{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794222358,"nonce":"ZQwkggfq3c7O3aI/haX8Rlq0m18=","title":"jno.fdm re-traces and re-compiles the whole march on every solve()","message":"Each transient fdm.solve() builds a new SemidiscreteTimeBlock in _run_block, and the march cache (backend_blocks._cached_march) lives on the block, so a second solve of the same problem with value-equal scheme and solver specs never hits it. In a cProfile of a warm bdf2 solve of a 2-D Brusselator (32x32, 100 steps, lu()), make_jaxpr/trace_to_jaxpr and backend_compile take about half of the solve. jno.fem keeps its block on the operator and does not show this. Test: tests/test_fdm.py::test_repeated_march_is_traced_once.","files":null}]}